PREVIEW(1)                  Funny CLI Manual                  PREVIEW(1)

NAME
    preview — Preview the beginning of a file, because sometimes
              "cat" is a commitment and you just want a sneak peek.

SYNOPSIS
    preview <file> [lines]

DESCRIPTION
    The 'preview' command displays the first portion of a text file
    through the CLI's pager.

    By default, it shows the first 25 lines.

    Unlike 'cat', which enthusiastically dumps the entire file onto
    your terminal, 'preview' understands the concept of moderation.

    It's basically saying:

        "Let's see what we're dealing with before we commit."

ARGUMENTS
    file
        The file to preview.

        Required. If omitted, the command provides usage instructions
        and previews absolutely nothing.

    lines
        The maximum number of lines to preview.

        Optional. Defaults to 25.

        Increase this when 25 lines aren't enough to establish the
        situation. Decrease it when they are already too many.

OUTPUT
    The requested number of lines are passed to the CLI pager.

    This means the output may be displayed in a paginated or
    otherwise interactive manner, depending on how 'pager_lines'
    is implemented.

    In other words, 'preview' doesn't just throw everything at your
    face. It attempts to be civilized.

ERRORS
    preview error: <error>
        Something went wrong while opening or previewing the file.

        Possible causes include:
        - The file doesn't exist.
        - Permission denied.
        - The path is invalid.
        - The file contains something the filesystem would rather
          not discuss.

USAGE ERRORS
    > preview

        Usage: preview <file> [lines]

        You requested a preview without telling the command what
        to preview.

    > preview README.md
        Shows the first 25 lines of README.md.

        Enough to decide whether this README is worth reading.

    > preview README.md 5
        Shows only the first 5 lines.

        The executive summary of the executive summary.

    > preview application.log 100
        Shows up to 100 lines through the pager.

        You've gone from "preview" to "investigation."

FUN FACTS
    - The default preview size is 25 lines.
    - Output is sent through 'pager_lines', rather than printed
      directly.
    - Files are opened as UTF-8 text.
    - Invalid characters are replaced rather than causing a meltdown.
    - File completion is enabled, because tab completion knows
      filenames better than you do.
    - A preview is technically just looking at the beginning of
      something before deciding whether you regret opening it.
    - 'cat' shows you everything.
    - 'preview' has boundaries.

